[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   step_062: Planet Nine insertion test -- does the published perturber
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   produce the observed comet anomaly on real trajectories?
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   step_042 established that subtracting the measured planetary baseline
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   leaves the in-cap anomaly undiminished.  This step asks the inverse
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   question for the specific conventional hypothesis: insert the Brown &
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   Batygin (2021, AJ 162, 219) Planet Nine into the same backward
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   integrations and measure what it does to each comet's reconstructed
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   orbit.
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   Two published realizations are tested:
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   bb21_ml   maximum-likelihood model: m9 = 5.0 M_earth, a9 = 300 AU,
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   e9 = 0.15, i9 = 17 deg, varpi9 = 254 deg, Om9 = 108 deg
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   (BB21 Section on maximum likelihood, "nearly a local peak
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   in every dimension")
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   bb21_med  marginalized-median model: m9 = 6.9 M_earth, a9 = 461 AU,
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   e9 = 0.30, i9 = 15.6 deg, varpi9 = 246.7 deg, Om9 = 96.9 deg
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   (BB21 corner-plot medians)
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   P9's mean anomaly is unconstrained by the secular analysis (BB21 set
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   M9 = 0 and marginalized the position), so each model is run on a
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   four-point mean-anomaly grid {0, 90, 180, 270 deg}; M9 = 180 deg
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   (near apoapsis) is the residence-time-weighted most probable position
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   for an eccentric orbit.  This brackets every plausible placement.
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   For each class-1 CODE comet (identical selection to step_040/042) the
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   osculating elements at the catalogued perihelion epoch are converted
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   to a heliocentric state and integrated backward through Sun +
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   planetary-system barycentres (DE440s) to 255 AU heliocentric, twice:
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   with and without the P9 particle (REBOUND/IAS15).  At the boundary the
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   osculating periapsis direction and barycentric 1/a are recovered for
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   each run.  The paired differences
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   drot_p9  = angle between boundary periapsis directions, P9 vs no-P9
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   dk_p9    = |1/a_out(P9) - 1/a_out(noP9)|   [10^-6 AU^-1]
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   denc_p9  = minimum comet-P9 distance [AU]
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   isolate the perturbation P9 would actually inject into the catalogued
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   original-orbit reconstruction.  The observed discrepancy d_of is the
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   orig->fut perihelion-direction residual used by every Phase-3 step.
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   Tests per (model, M9) cell and pooled:
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   1. magnitude: median/max drot_p9 against the observed in-cap median
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   d_of -- the trajectory-level impulse budget;
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   2. targeting: Spearman(drot_p9, d_of) and in/out-cap Mann-Whitney on
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   drot_p9 -- a causal perturber must hit the discrepant comets;
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   3. absorption: log(d_of) ~ drot_p9 + |kick_e| + q residual cap
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   contrast -- if P9 explained the signal the residual collapses.
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   Outputs
[2026-09-21 14:37:22 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 062]   results/step_b27_planet_nine_insertion.json
